From 817acff84ca433f393f572745dfbd4990d2ab13e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:41:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] nv50: only push constant buffer updates through a current
 binding

nv50_cb_push() writes small constant buffer updates with CB_ADDR and
CB_DATA, which reach the buffer through a hardware binding point rather
than through its address. It takes the binding point from
res->cb_bindings, which is set when a binding is validated and can be
out of date in two ways:

- The buffer's storage was reallocated, as when an application orphans
  a busy buffer with glBufferData(NULL) and then updates it. The binding
  is marked dirty, but until the next draw validates it the hardware
  still points at the old storage, so the update goes there and is
  lost.
- Another context has bound a different buffer to the same binding
  point. nv50 contexts share the channel's 3D state and
  res->cb_bindings is not per context, so the update lands in the other
  context's buffer.

GTK 4's ngl renderer does both: each window and popover has its own GL
context, and every frame orphans and updates a small uniform buffer
with the projection for that surface. With a popover open, the window
and the popover are drawn with each other's projection, and menus show
shrunken or stretched content.

Only use a binding point when this context's state is on the hardware,
the binding has been validated since it last changed, and it still
points at this buffer. Otherwise write through the buffer's address, as
is already done for buffers that are not bound.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_transfer.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_transfer.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_transfer.c
index a1e3082..002f76e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_transfer.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv50/nv50_transfer.c
@@ -540,16 +540,27 @@ nv50_cb_push(struct nouveau_context *nv,
    struct nv50_context *nv50 = nv50_context(&nv->pipe);
    struct nv50_constbuf *cb = NULL;
    int s, bufid;
+   /* CB_DATA writes through a binding point, not to the buffer's address,
+    * and res->cb_bindings is shared by all contexts. Only use a binding
+    * point that this context has emitted, that is still on the hardware and
+    * that still points at this buffer: another context may have bound a
+    * different buffer to the same slot since.
+    */
+   const bool hw_state_ours = nv50->screen->cur_ctx == nv50;
+
    /* Go through all the constbuf binding points of this buffer and try to
     * find one which contains the region to be updated.
     */
-   for (s = 0; s < NV50_MAX_SHADER_STAGES && !cb; s++) {
-      uint16_t bindings = res->cb_bindings[s];
+   for (s = 0; hw_state_ours && s < NV50_MAX_SHADER_STAGES && !cb; s++) {
+      uint16_t bindings = res->cb_bindings[s] & ~nv50->constbuf_dirty[s];
       while (bindings) {
          int i = ffs(bindings) - 1;
          uint32_t cb_offset = nv50->constbuf[s][i].offset;
 
          bindings &= ~(1 << i);
+         if (nv50->constbuf[s][i].user ||
+             nv50->constbuf[s][i].u.buf != &res->base)
+            continue;
          if (cb_offset <= offset &&
              cb_offset + nv50->constbuf[s][i].size >= offset + words * 4) {
             cb = &nv50->constbuf[s][i];
